---
import Shell from '../components/Martlet.astro';import {localPath as href} from '../paths';
const page={id:'setup',title:'Make it your own.',eyebrow:'Template guide',summary:'A native Astro project, with the canonical Martlet shell and editable content.'};
---
<Shell page={page} href={href} base={import.meta.env.BASE_URL} renderContent={false}><h2>Run locally</h2><pre><code>npm install
npm run dev</code></pre><h2>Build for hosting</h2><pre><code>npm run build</code></pre><p>Publish <code>dist</code> to a static host. Set <code>NIGHTJAR_BASE=/preview/</code> to build beneath a path prefix.</p><h2>Edit the content</h2><p>Set the site name and navigation in the native SourceHeader component. Edit page content in <code>src/pages</code> and the shared fictional records in <code>page-archetypes/content/catalog.json</code>.</p><h2>Inspect the native components</h2><p>The reference includes working component examples: <a href={href('/article/')}>an article</a>, <a href={href('/documentation/')}>documentation</a>, <a href={href('/layouts/')}>the layout lab</a>, and <a href={href('/form/')}>registration with recovery and reset</a>.</p><h2>Keep the contract</h2><p>The approved imagery, credits, local fonts and family styles are included with this reference. Keep their provenance with derivatives. Interactive specimens are browser-local demonstrations; read the <a href={href('/examples/integrations/')}>integration boundaries</a> before connecting a real service.</p></Shell>
